<p>When you run this code, GORM will:</p>
<ol>
<li>Check if the tables exist, and create them if they don&#x27;t</li>
<li>Add missing columns to existing tables</li>
<li>Create indexes and constraints</li>
<li>Establish foreign key relationships between tables</li>
</ol>
<p>The <code>AutoMigrate</code> function works by comparing your Go struct definitions to the actual database schema and making necessary changes to align them. It accepts a list of model struct pointers and returns an error if something goes wrong.</p>
<p>Note that <code>AutoMigrate</code> only adds things that are missing; it won&#x27;t delete columns or tables that exist in the database but not in your models. This is a safety feature to prevent accidental data loss.</p>
<p>This will create the necessary tables if they don&#x27;t exist and update them to match your model definitions.</p>
