<li>For each batch, GORM calls the provided callback function with the batch results</li>
<li>Inside the callback, we process each result individually</li>
</ol>
<p>Batch processing is particularly important when dealing with operations that might affect millions of records, such as data migrations, report generation, or bulk updates. It&#x27;s also useful when you need to perform complex processing on each record that might be resource-intensive.</p>
<p>For more information on batch processing and other advanced querying techniques, refer to the <a class="group inline" href="https://gorm.io/docs/advanced_query.html#FindInBatches" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GORM documentation<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a>.</p>
